PegResponsiveIrm::constructor(address,CurveConfig,address)
├── given initialOwner is the zero address
│   ├── it should revert with OwnableInvalidOwner(address(0))
│   ├── it should reject before checking oracle or configuration inputs
│   └── it should not emit any surviving events
└── given initialOwner is non-zero
    ├── when oracle is the zero address
    │   ├── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidOracle
    │   ├── it should reject before validating the configuration
    │   └── it should not emit any surviving events
    └── when oracle is non-zero
        ├── given the price configuration is invalid
        │   ├── when stressPrice is zero
        │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidPriceConfig
        │   ├── when recoveryPrice is greater than MAX_RECOVERY_PRICE
        │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidPriceConfig
        │   ├── when stressPrice equals recoveryPrice
        │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidPriceConfig
        │   └── when stressPrice is greater than recoveryPrice
        │       └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidPriceConfig
        ├── given the price configuration is valid and the rate configuration is invalid
        │   ├── when baseRate is zero
        │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
        │   ├── when baseRate is greater than stressRate
        │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
        │   ├── when stressRate equals maxRate
        │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
        │   ├── when stressRate is greater than maxRate
        │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
        │   └── when maxRate is greater than MAX_BORROW_RATE
        │       └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
        ├── given the price and rate configuration are valid and the controller configuration is invalid
        │   ├── when doublingDistance is zero
        │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidControllerConfig
        │   ├── when recoveryDelay is zero
        │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidControllerConfig
        │   └── when maxOracleAge is zero
        │       └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidControllerConfig
        ├── given more than one configuration group is invalid
        │   ├── when the price group is invalid
        │   │   └── it should prioritize PegResponsiveIrmInvalidPriceConfig
        │   └── when the price group is valid and both rate and controller groups are invalid
        │       └── it should prioritize PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
        └── given every configuration group is valid
            ├── when stressPrice is one and recoveryPrice is two
            │   └── it should accept the minimum non-zero ordered price thresholds
            ├── when stressPrice equals recoveryPrice minus one
            │   └── it should accept the immediate valid side of the strict price ordering
            ├── when recoveryPrice equals MAX_RECOVERY_PRICE
            │   └── it should deploy successfully
            ├── when baseRate is one
            │   └── it should accept the minimum non-zero base rate
            ├── when baseRate equals stressRate
            │   └── it should deploy successfully
            ├── when maxRate equals stressRate plus one
            │   └── it should accept the immediate valid side of the strict rate ordering
            ├── when maxRate equals MAX_BORROW_RATE
            │   └── it should deploy successfully
            ├── when doublingDistance is one
            │   └── it should accept the minimum non-zero doubling distance
            ├── when recoveryDelay is one
            │   └── it should accept the minimum non-zero recovery delay
            ├── when maxOracleAge is one
            │   └── it should accept the minimum non-zero oracle age
            ├── when doublingDistance is type(uint256).max
            │   └── it should deploy successfully because doublingDistance has no upper validation bound
            ├── when recoveryDelay is type(uint48).max
            │   └── it should deploy successfully
            ├── when maxOracleAge is type(uint48).max
            │   └── it should deploy successfully
            ├── when maxOracleAge is less than recoveryDelay
            │   └── it should deploy successfully without enforcing a relationship between them
            ├── when maxOracleAge equals recoveryDelay
            │   └── it should deploy successfully without enforcing a relationship between them
            ├── when maxOracleAge is greater than recoveryDelay
            │   └── it should deploy successfully without enforcing a relationship between them
            ├── when oracle has no code
            │   ├── it should deploy successfully
            │   └── it should not call getPrice or otherwise validate the oracle implementation
            ├── it should store oracle and every CurveConfig field exactly
            ├── it should set market to the zero address
            ├── it should initialize IRState with borrowRate equal to baseRate
            ├── it should initialize lastUpdate and recoveryStartedAt to zero and stressMode to false
            ├── it should set owner to initialOwner and pendingOwner to the zero address
            ├── it should emit OwnershipTransferred(address(0), initialOwner)
            ├── it should then emit SetPegOracle(address(0), oracle)
            ├── it should then emit SetCurveConfig(config)
            ├── it should then emit IRStateUpdated(initialState)
            └── it should not emit StressStateUpdated or BorrowRateUpdated
